      description: "Donald Ross Sportswear borrows the name of one of golf's most revered architects to anchor a brand rooted in traditional American golf style. Founded in 2008 and headquartered in Aberdeen, North Carolina—near Pinehurst, where Ross himself designed the famed No. 2 course—the brand emphasizes premium fabrics, classic silhouettes, and course-ready styling that appeals to golfers who value heritage over hype. Donald Ross Sportswear produces polos, outerwear, pants, and layering pieces designed with refined details: mother-of-pearl buttons, fine-gauge knits, and tailored fits that feel more country club than athleisure. The brand targets affluent, traditional golfers and has built distribution through high-end pro shops, private clubs, and resort courses. Its aesthetic is deliberate and conservative, favoring timeless design over seasonal trends. While not as widely recognized as FootJoy or Polo Golf, Donald Ross has cultivated a loyal following among players who prioritize quality construction and understated elegance. The brand's positioning as a premium American label aligns it with the legacy of Donald Ross himself, whose courses remain some of the most respected in the world. In recent years, the brand has faced competition from both established heritage labels and newer direct-to-consumer players, but it continues to occupy a distinct lane: classic American golf apparel built for golfers who see the game as an extension of a particular lifestyle. Donald Ross Sportswear represents a segment of the market that values tradition, craftsmanship, and the kind of quiet luxury that doesn't need to announce itself.",
