      allCategories: ["Clubs & Balls"],
      subCategories: ["Clubs"],
      description: "MacGregor is one of golf's oldest and most storied equipment brands, founded in 1897 in Dayton, Ohio. The company built its legacy through the mid-20th century, producing clubs used by some of the game's greatest players, including Jack Nicklaus, who played MacGregor irons and woods during his dominant years in the 1960s and 70s. The brand's Eye-O-Matic woods and forged irons became iconic symbols of golf's golden era, representing craftsmanship and tour-level performance.\n\nAfter decades of ownership changes and market shifts, MacGregor's influence waned as newer brands like TaylorMade and Callaway dominated equipment innovation. The name changed hands multiple times, passing through various corporate owners before landing with Golf Brands Inc., which now operates the brand from Albany, Georgia. Today's MacGregor produces a range of clubs and equipment aimed primarily at recreational golfers and international markets where the name still carries historical weight.\n\nMacGregor's modern offerings include complete club sets, individual irons, and golf balls, often positioned as value-oriented alternatives to the major equipment manufacturers. The brand leverages its heritage in marketing but lacks the R&D budgets, tour presence, and retail footprint of industry leaders. MacGregor clubs are more commonly found in discount channels, overseas markets, and among golfers seeking affordable options with a recognizable name.\n\nThe brand's story is emblematic of golf's equipment industry consolidation. Where MacGregor once competed at the highest level of innovation and tour validation, it now exists as a heritage nameplate serving a different segment of the market. For collectors and historians, vintage MacGregor equipment remains highly sought after—a reminder of the brand's legitimate golden age. For today's buyers, it's a budget-friendly option trading on a name that once meant something very different.",
