      subCategories: ["Shafts"],
      description: "Newton Golf is a California-based shaft manufacturer founded in 2020 under the Sacks Parente Golf umbrella, a company known for its engineering-forward approach to golf equipment. Unlike legacy shaft brands that rely heavily on tour validation or incremental tweaks, Newton positions itself around first-principles physics—analyzing how mass distribution, torque, and energy transfer affect clubhead delivery and ball flight. The brand's messaging emphasizes measurable performance gains through thoughtful engineering rather than marketing hype or pro endorsements.\n\nNewton's product line focuses on driver and fairway shafts designed to optimize energy transfer from the player's swing into the clubhead. The brand uses proprietary materials and construction techniques intended to reduce inconsistency and improve repeatability, targeting both club fitters and discerning players willing to invest in custom builds. Newton shafts are typically positioned in the premium segment, competing with established names like Fujikura, Graphite Design, and Mitsubishi in the fitting bay rather than on retail racks.\n\nBecause Newton launched relatively recently, it lacks the decades of tour history that define brands like True Temper or Project X. Instead, it has built credibility through partnerships with club fitters and performance-focused custom builders who appreciate its data-driven design philosophy. The brand appeals to players who view equipment as a system of optimized components rather than off-the-shelf solutions—those who are willing to experiment with shaft profiles to unlock marginal gains. In an industry often driven by legacy and feel, Newton represents a newer wave of golf companies built on engineering transparency and performance validation, aiming to earn trust through physics rather than pedigree.",
