      category: "Bags & Accessories",
      allCategories: ["Bags & Accessories"],
      subCategories: ["Bags"],
      description: "Ogio, founded in 1987 in Bluffdale, Utah, and now part of Topgolf Callaway Brands, produces golf bags, travel gear, and accessories known for bold styling, durable construction, and functional innovation. The brand originated outside golf, building its reputation in motocross and action sports with rugged, high-performance bags before expanding into golf in the mid-1990s. That heritage is evident in Ogio's design language—aggressive colorways, technical fabrics, and organizational features that appeal to golfers who want gear that stands out on the course and performs under heavy use.\n\nOgio's golf bag lineup includes stand bags, cart bags, and staff bags engineered with features like integrated cooler pockets, reinforced legs, multiple dividers, and weather-resistant materials. The brand has introduced several notable innovations over the years, including the Silencer cart bag, designed with sound-dampening materials to reduce club rattle, and the Fuse stand bag series, which emphasizes lightweight construction without sacrificing storage capacity. Ogio's aesthetic skews younger and more athletic than legacy bag brands like Sun Mountain or Titleist, appealing to players who prioritize style and functionality over traditional country club conservatism.\n\nBeyond bags, Ogio produces golf-adjacent travel gear, including duffel bags, shoe bags, and luggage designed for golfers who travel frequently to courses or tournaments. The brand's integration into Callaway's portfolio has expanded its retail presence and distribution, though it maintains a distinct identity separate from Callaway Golf's core equipment business. Ogio targets golfers who view their gear as an extension of personal style and who appreciate technical details that enhance the on-course experience—players who want bags that look sharp, organize efficiently, and hold up to the wear of regular play.",
