      allCategories: ["Tech & Training Aids"],
      subCategories: ["Swing Training"],
      description: "PuttOut disrupted the putting training aid category when it launched from London in 2016 with a compact device that simulates realistic green conditions through physics-based design. The company's flagship Pressure Putt Trainer features a curved ramp that returns perfectly struck putts while rejecting mishits, providing immediate feedback on strike quality and pace control. Unlike traditional putting aids that simply create targets, PuttOut's design replicates the ball behavior golfers experience on actual greens, making practice more transferable to on-course performance. The device's portability and minimal footprint made it ideal for home practice, contributing to rapid adoption among golfers seeking effective training tools that don't require dedicated space. PuttOut expanded its product line to include putting mats, mirrors, gates, and other training accessories, building a comprehensive putting practice ecosystem. The brand's success stems from solving a legitimate problem—most putting practice doesn't replicate real conditions—with thoughtful design rather than gimmicky features. PuttOut gained credibility through endorsements from teaching professionals and tour players who recognized its utility in developing consistent stroke mechanics and distance control. The company's British heritage and design-focused approach distinguish it from American competitors, though its products have achieved global distribution through online channels and specialty retailers. PuttOut represents the successful application of engineering principles to golf training, creating tools that provide measurable improvement rather than false confidence. The brand's growth during golf's pandemic boom accelerated awareness, but its sustained relevance depends on product quality and effectiveness rather than trend-driven demand. For golfers serious about improving their putting, PuttOut offers scientifically sound training aids that deliver on their performance promises.",
