      subCategories: ["Trendy/Lifestyle"],
      description: "Quiet Golf emerged from Los Angeles in 2020 as a deliberate counterpoint to the increasingly loud, logo-heavy direction of modern golf lifestyle brands. Founded during the pandemic golf boom, the brand tapped into a growing appetite for understated golf apparel that borrowed aesthetic cues from skate, surf, and streetwear culture rather than traditional country club styling or maximalist hype brands.\n\nThe brand's design philosophy centers on minimalist graphics, muted color palettes, and relaxed silhouettes that feel equally at home on the course or at the skatepark. Quiet Golf's polos, tees, and outerwear typically feature subtle branding and vintage-inspired treatments, avoiding the bold patterns and tech-forward fabrics that dominate mainstream golf apparel. The aesthetic draws comparison to brands like Stüssy or Carhartt WIP—heritage workwear and streetwear influences recontextualized for golf.\n\nQuiet Golf operates primarily direct-to-consumer through its website and social media, building community through content that emphasizes personal style over performance metrics. The brand positions itself for golfers who prioritize authenticity and subcultural credibility over technical specifications or tour validation. Pricing sits in the accessible-premium range, typically lower than luxury golf brands but higher than mass-market options.\n\nThe brand represents a specific lane in golf's ongoing cultural expansion: the intersection of action sports, streetwear, and golf that appeals to younger players who came to the game through non-traditional pathways. While Quiet Golf lacks the tour presence or retail distribution of established players, it has carved out a loyal following among golfers seeking alternatives to both traditional golf brands and the louder end of the lifestyle golf spectrum. In a market increasingly crowded with new golf apparel brands, Quiet Golf's commitment to understated design and subcultural authenticity distinguishes its positioning.",
