      subCategories: ["Bags"],
      description: "Stitch Golf launched in 2012 with a focus on premium golf bags that blend minimalist design with luxury materials, carving out space in a category long dominated by functional but uninspired options. Based in North Carolina's golf manufacturing corridor, the brand initially made its name with stand bags and cart bags featuring clean lines, premium leather accents, and thoughtful organizational details that appealed to golfers tired of logo-heavy, overly technical designs. Stitch bags are built in limited runs with attention to colorways and materials—waxed canvas, full-grain leather, and water-resistant fabrics—that reference heritage luggage and outdoor gear rather than traditional golf aesthetics. The company has since expanded into apparel, headwear, and accessories, maintaining the same design philosophy: understated, well-made, and free of the garish branding common in golf. Stitch's pricing reflects its premium positioning, with bags often exceeding $400 and apparel priced comparably to luxury golf brands. The brand has developed a following among younger, style-conscious golfers and has collaborated with courses, clubs, and events on co-branded limited editions. Stitch operates primarily direct-to-consumer through its website, though select golf shops and resorts carry the line. The brand's growth coincides with a broader shift in golf toward design-forward products that don't sacrifice performance for aesthetics. While Stitch lacks the scale or tour presence of major equipment brands, it has successfully positioned itself as the golf bag of choice for golfers who view their equipment as an extension of personal style. In a category where Sun Mountain and Vessel dominate, Stitch offers a quieter, more refined alternative.",
