      founded: 1981,
      parentCompany: "Sun Mountain Sports",
      category: "Bags & Accessories",
      allCategories: ["Bags & Accessories"],
      subCategories: ["Bags"],
      description: "Sun Mountain has operated from Missoula, Montana, since 1981 as one of the golf industry's most innovative manufacturers of bags, push carts, and outerwear. The company pioneered the modern stand bag in the 1980s and has maintained a reputation for functional design aimed at golfers who walk rather than ride. Sun Mountain's product line emphasizes lightweight materials, thoughtful organization, and durability suited to the demands of walking 18 holes regularly. The C-130 and 4.5 LS stand bags are perennial bestsellers, known for balancing weight, storage, and stability. Sun Mountain also dominates the push cart category with its Speed Cart and Micro-Cart lines, which fold compactly and feature smooth-rolling wheels and intuitive controls. The company's outerwear, particularly its rain gear, is widely regarded as some of the best in golf, built for serious weather rather than occasional drizzle. Sun Mountain operates as a true manufacturer rather than a brand that outsources production, maintaining control over design and quality. The company supplies private-label bags for other brands and courses, giving it scale beyond its own branding. Sun Mountain's aesthetic is functional rather than flashy—bags are often understated, with clean lines and muted colors—which appeals to traditional golfers but lacks the design-forward appeal of newer brands like Vessel or Stitch. The brand has a strong presence among serious amateur golfers, particularly those who prioritize walking and view their bag as a piece of equipment rather than a fashion statement. As walking culture has grown and push carts have become more socially acceptable, Sun Mountain has benefited from its decades of focus on these categories.",
