      allCategories: ["Apparel & Footwear"],
      subCategories: ["Trendy/Lifestyle", "Women's"],
      description: "Byrdie Golf Social Wear launched from Charlotte, North Carolina in 2021 with an aesthetic that looks backward to move forward—mining vintage golf style for inspiration while translating it through contemporary women's fashion. The brand name itself signals the dual identity: serious enough about golf to build a company around it, but focused on the social, lifestyle, and style dimensions of the sport rather than pure performance. Collections feature patterns, silhouettes, and design references drawn from golf's preppy heyday—think 1970s and 80s golf fashion—but updated with modern fits, fabrics, and styling. The result is apparel that feels more at home on Instagram than in a traditional pro shop, designed for women who view golf as part of a curated lifestyle and social experience. Byrdie's pieces are built to transition seamlessly from course to brunch to errands, reflecting how younger women actually wear and think about golf clothing. The brand has leaned into community building and social media, understanding that for its target customer, golf apparel is as much about identity and belonging as about technical performance. This positions Byrdie in the growing lifestyle/fashion segment of women's golf apparel, competing less with traditional performance brands and more with fashion-forward labels and athleisure companies entering golf. The approach resonates with women who came to golf during the pandemic boom, who often prioritize style and social experience over competitive play, and who expect their golf wardrobe to integrate with their broader closet. While Byrdie lacks the technical credentials or tour presence of established brands, it reflects an important shift in women's golf—the increasing centrality of style, community, and lifestyle rather than purely athletic performance.",
