      category: "Apparel & Footwear",
      allCategories: ["Apparel & Footwear"],
      subCategories: ["Performance", "Women's"],
      description: "Kastel Denmark carries a misleading name—it's headquartered in Reno, Nevada, not Scandinavia—but the brand's origin story is rooted in urgency rather than geography. Founded in 2012 after a skin cancer diagnosis threatened its founder's equestrian career, Kastel was built around serious sun protection, specifically UPF 30 and 50 fabrics designed for athletes who spend extended hours outdoors. The brand began in the horse world, where long-sleeved sun shirts are standard equipment, but quickly crossed over into golf and tennis as awareness of UV exposure grew among outdoor sports participants. Kastel's signature products are long-sleeve performance tops and quarter-zips featuring bold prints, vibrant colorways, and technical fabrics that wick moisture while blocking harmful rays. The brand has developed a cult following among women who prioritize both protection and personality, offering designs that range from tropical florals to geometric patterns that stand out in a category often dominated by solid pastels. Kastel competes in the intersection of performance and lifestyle, appealing to consumers who want functional apparel that doesn't look clinical. Distribution includes both equestrian and golf retail channels, with particularly strong presence in Florida, California, and the Southwest where sun protection is a year-round concern. The brand has expanded beyond shirts into hats, leggings, and accessories, all maintaining the same UPF-first philosophy. Kastel's positioning is premium but not luxury—pieces typically retail between $80-120, positioning them as investment items justified by health benefits and durability. The brand lacks tour visibility but thrives through grassroots adoption among teaching professionals, club members, and multi-sport athletes who appreciate apparel designed with medical rationale, not just marketing.",
