      allCategories: ["Apparel & Footwear"],
      subCategories: ["Luxury/High-End", "Women's"],
      description: "Williams Athletic Club emerged in 2022 as a direct answer to what founder Emily Williams saw as a persistent gap in women's golf: apparel that treated female golfers as athletes who appreciate understated luxury rather than defaulting to overly feminine or garish styling. Based in Lake Oswego, Oregon, the brand operates in the quiet luxury segment of golf wear, a positioning that has gained traction as golf's demographic shifts toward younger, style-conscious women seeking alternatives to traditional golf brands.\n\nThe brand's aesthetic centers on refined minimalism—think neutral color palettes, clean lines, and premium fabrications that wouldn't look out of place at a country club or a contemporary art gallery. Williams Athletic Club produces performance polos, tailored trousers, midlayers, and skorts constructed from technical fabrics that deliver moisture-wicking and stretch without announcing their performance credentials through logos or loud branding. The company's signature pieces include its signature polo with a subtly elevated collar and fitted silhouette, and its pleated performance skort that bridges traditional golf style with modern tailoring.\n\nWhile Williams Athletic Club doesn't chase tour endorsements or flashy collaborations, its growth reflects broader industry trends. The women's golf apparel market has seen significant investment and innovation since 2020, driven by increased female participation and demand for options beyond pink-and-purple pastels or shrunken versions of men's designs. Williams Athletic Club competes in a space alongside brands like Greyson's women's line and G/FORE, but distinguishes itself through its exclusively female focus and quieter, less logo-driven approach.\n\nThe brand sells direct-to-consumer through its website and select premium golf retailers. Its Lake Oswego headquarters positions it within the Pacific Northwest's emerging golf culture, where outdoor lifestyle brands have long embraced minimalist design and quality-first positioning. For female golfers seeking wardrobe staples that prioritize fit, fabric, and timeless style over trend-chasing, Williams Athletic Club offers a clear alternative in an increasingly crowded market.",
